course: dictionary
lesson: 7221
title: Phosphorus, the element that glows
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Phosphorus is a chemical element. Scientists write it with the symbol P, and its atomic number is 15. Every element has its own number like this, so we can tell them apart.
explain: Phosphorus is a non-metal, and all living things need it. It is in our bones, teeth and DNA, the code that tells our bodies how to grow. Plants need it too, so it helps them grow.
explain: «Striking a match makes heat by friction; safety matches light only on the box strip, which holds red phosphorus.» Pure white phosphorus is very dangerous because it catches fire by itself in air. Red phosphorus is safer, so it is used on matchboxes.
explain: «Farmers add nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium to soil as fertiliser to grow more food.» Scientists write these three plant foods as N-P-K, with P standing for phosphorus. Context helps you see that P here means a plant food.
fact: Phosphorus is a chemical element with the symbol P and atomic number 15.
fact: Phosphorus is a non-metal that all living things need.
fact: Phosphorus is found in our bones, teeth and DNA.
fact: White phosphorus glows in the dark and catches fire by itself in air, so it is very dangerous.
fact: The word comes from Greek for "light-bringer", because it glows.
exercise: What is the chemical symbol for phosphorus? | Ph | Po | Phos | *P
exercise: Where is phosphorus found in our bodies? | *In our bones and teeth | In our blood only, not in bones | In our hair and nails only | In our eyes
exercise: «Pure white phosphorus catches fire by itself in air.» What does this tell us? | It is safe to play with | It is only found in plants | *It is very dangerous | It is a metal that never burns
test: Why is the name phosphorus linked to light? | Because it is a shiny metal like gold | Because it is used in torches only | *Because it glows | Because it lights up homes
test: Why is red phosphorus used on matchboxes? | It makes the matches taste sweet | It is the only metal that can be struck | It is a cheap paint | *It is safer than white phosphorus
exam: Which statement about phosphorus is true? | It is a type of sugar | It is only found in the sea | It is a metal that never reacts with anything | *It is a non-metal that all living things need
